        "title": "A sprawling Hindu holy site.",
        "text": "A short taxi ride from central Kathmandu, Pashupatinath is a large complex of temples, with monkeys darting about all, that gives a fascinating taste of Nepal's Hindu traditions. The 1000 rupee cat to enter does not allow non-Hindus to enter the main temple, but views within can be archived from the hills surrounding. Beware the touts and guides and sadhus who will ask for contributions for any device rendered and just wander the site, cross the river and meander the peaceful parks behind (which are also the starting point for another 20 minute trek that will take you to the Boudhanath Stupa Buddhist site).",
