        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r423041812-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Har Har Mahadev",
        "text": "What a surreal experience. Apart from the sense of peace and tranquillity that this temple has to offer, the lack of commercialization makes this a very pleasant place of worship. No one hounding you for money, no one pushing you around asking you to hurry with your worship and a general sensibility amongst most devotees lets you be with yourself, in the presence of the lord, even in a large crowd. Monkeys, Rams, Calves, Dogs, Pigeons roam about freely in the concourse thus making it such a beautiful sight to see. It screams of peace and oneness with the divine. One of the most peaceful experiences that I have had in a long time. It could be a little cleaner though. Having said that, I travelled during the monsoon and soon after a sort of a downpour - so expecting the place to be dry was a little bit of a stretch. A must place to visit.",
