        "title": "Must visit place for pilgrimage",
        "text": "This is one of the world heritage site located about 10 min drive from Tribhuban International Airport at Kathmandu. Very well maintained and clean. One can visit the temple without any usually hassled by touts. The temple is located in the bank of river Bagmati. You can spend some good time in the temple premise, it should take about an hour or so to go around the temple properly. Special puja can be arranged on prior bookings. Saturday and Monday are usually most crowded days as locals visit the temple on these days. Usually the temple is open for darshan from 7-11 AM.",
