        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r420687513-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Holy place",
        "text": "One of the holiest place for Hindus. Non-hindus are not allowed to enter the main temple premises but there are a lot of other places to see here.\n\nThere is a stairway leading towards another temple just behind the Pashupati temple. Climb the stairs and you will find a place to sit and enjoy the view. It is just wonderful to just sit there and gaze at everything thats going around. The place si crowded in evening and on holidays. Climb to top of the stairs to see some artistic temple with religious significance. The 2015 Earthquake did quite a lot of damage to the temples but they are still standing.\n\nNote : Try and go to the temple in evening(just before sunset) and ask anyone for 'evening aarati'. It is done everyday and is one of the hidden gems in Kathmandu. A must see.",
